### SKILL.md  [instructions]
- Ralph Loop is a task execution discipline that turns the AI agent into a self-running sprint machine. For every user task, the AI creates a structured persistent memory file at `/workspace/memory/ralph-loop.md` and follows it until the job is done — checking off each step, updating progress, and sending brief human-readable updates after each completed phase.
- The name comes from the Ralph Wiggum principle (The Simpsons): the AI keeps going, never gives up, and iterates until it succeeds.
- - Any multi-step task where the user expects autonomous execution without questions
