- ## Ralph Loop Protocol — Step by Step
- ### PHASE 1: Init (one-time at start)
- 1. **Create the file** at `/workspace/memory/ralph-loop.md` with the full plan
- 2. **Set status** to `🟡 In Progress`
- 3. **Send initial Telegram message** to the user (short confirmation, 1-2 sentences):
-    > "🚀 *Task name* — Ralph Loop started. *Brief description of what will happen*. Checkpoint file created."
- ### PHASE 2: Execute (main loop)
- 2. Work the step (write code, run commands, create files, etc.)
- 4. If the step has sub-steps (micro-tasks discovered during work), add them as indented sub-items
- 5. If the step is a logical **phase boundary** (a group of 2-4 related sub-steps forming one coherent unit), then:
-    - Update "Current Work" section
-    - Add to "Progress Log" with timestamp
-    - **Send Telegram update** (2 sentences max, no questions asked):
-      > "✅ *[Phase name]* — *[what is done]*. *Next: [what's next]*."
- 6. If the entire task is done → jump to Phase 3
- ### PHASE 2B: If Stuck
- If an error occurs and I cannot resolve it within 2 attempts:
- 1. **Do not retry infinitely** — that wastes time and resources
- 2. Write to the "Stalled / Blockers" section in `ralph-loop.md`:
-    ```
-    ```
-    🚧 [HH:MM UTC] — Step N: [exact error message or reason why stuck]
- 3. **Set status to `⏸️ Paused — Awaiting Input`**
- 4. **Send Telegram message:**
-    > "⏸️ *Ralph Loop paused* — *Step N failed: [brief one-line reason]*. *How do you want to proceed?*"
- 5. **Wait for your response** — we solve it together, then I resume
- 6. **Never skip a step** just to move forward — getting unblocked is the priority
- 1. Set status in file to `✅ Done`
- 2. Add completion note with final timestamp
- 3. **Delete `/workspace/memory/ralph-loop.md`** — no clutter left behind
- 4. **Send final Telegram message** (3-4 sentences):
-    > "🎉 *Task name* — done. *[What was produced/achieved]*. Files at: *[/workspace/path]*."
- 5. Done. Wait for next task.
- **Note:** On completion, the Ralph Loop file is DELETED automatically. No lingering working files. Old loops are preserved as `/workspace/memory/ralph-loop-YYYY-MM-DD.md` only if you explicitly ask to keep them.
- | Rule | Why |
- |------|-----|
- | Never ask the user questions during normal execution | The point is autonomous execution |
- | Always update the file after every step | Persistence is the key to the loop working |
- | **If stuck → stop, inform user, wait for solution together** | Ralph never gives up — but he also never pretends he has all the answers |
- | If user says "pause" → set status to `⏸️ Paused` | User may want to provide new input |
- | Break large steps into micro-steps (don't hesitate) | The finer the steps, the clearer the progress |
- | Every Telegram update is 2-3 sentences max | Telegram is not email — keep it punchy |
- | **Delete ralph-loop.md on completion** | No working files left behind |
- ## Example Telegram Updates (2-3 sentences each)
- **Good:**
- > "✅ Faza 1 — PDF generisan. Kreiran je novi Word dokument sa svim tabelama, zaglavljem u boji i cover stranom. Slede: faza 2."
- **Bad (too long, too much detail):**
- > "Zavrsio sam prvu fazu koja se ticala kreiranja PDF dokumenta na osnovu dostavljenog JSON-a. Koristio sam python-docx za generisanje tabele, zatim sam dodao novi stil za header..."
- **Too vague:**
- > "Nesto sam radio. Radim dalje."
- The loop ends when:
- - All steps in the plan are checked `[x]`
- - Status is set to `✅ Done`
- - Final message sent to user
- To start a new Ralph Loop for a different task, the old file is archived (renamed with date) and a new one is created. Old loops are kept as history.
